1
00:00:00,258 --> 00:00:02,807
Egypt's mightiest god had one weak spot:

2
00:00:02,897 --> 00:00:03,664
his name.

3
00:00:03,807 --> 00:00:05,281
And a goddess stole it.

4
00:00:05,701 --> 00:00:07,047
Ra says it himself:

5
00:00:07,148 --> 00:00:08,980
I am Khepera in the morning, Ra

6
00:00:08,791 --> 00:00:10,889
at noon, and Temu in the evening.

7
00:00:11,281 --> 00:00:13,321
But his secret name was hidden inside

8
00:00:13,133 --> 00:00:14,907
his body by his father and mother,

9
00:00:14,996 --> 00:00:16,828
so that no spell could master him.

10
00:00:17,237 --> 00:00:19,439
Isis knew words of power, and she

11
00:00:19,251 --> 00:00:20,956
wanted to be as great as Ra.

12
00:00:21,349 --> 00:00:23,644
She takes the old god's spittle, kneads

13
00:00:23,456 --> 00:00:24,362
it with dust…

14
00:00:24,405 --> 00:00:25,670
and makes a serpent.

15
00:00:26,073 --> 00:00:27,732
She lays it on his path.

16
00:00:27,898 --> 00:00:30,008
It bites him, and the living fire

17
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:30,876
leaves his body.

18
00:00:31,289 --> 00:00:33,526
Isis only heals him once Ra lets

19
00:00:33,338 --> 00:00:35,227
his name pass from his body into

20
00:00:35,039 --> 00:00:35,748
hers.

21
00:00:36,145 --> 00:00:37,630
Then she speaks the spell:

22
00:00:37,708 --> 00:00:39,077
flow, poison!

23
00:00:39,139 --> 00:00:40,034
Ra lives!

24
00:00:40,170 --> 00:00:41,423
The poison dies!

25
00:00:41,818 --> 00:00:44,009
Ever since, Isis is the Queen of

26
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:45,803
the gods, who knows Ra by his

27
00:00:45,614 --> 00:00:46,370
own name.

28
00:00:46,758 --> 00:00:48,277
Which text says so?

29
00:00:48,421 --> 00:00:50,855
An Egyptian papyrus kept in Turin.

30
00:00:51,253 --> 00:00:53,363
Save it, and send it to anyone

31
00:00:53,175 --> 00:00:54,972
who thinks Ra was invincible.

